<title>FRANCE: France's Bic buys Tipp-Ex of Germany.</title>
<headline>France's Bic buys Tipp-Ex of Germany.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>French pen and lighter manufacturer Bic said on Thursday that it had acquired Tipp-Ex Holding GmbH, which owns the German company that makes Tipp-Ex liquid eraser.</p>
<p>It did not disclose the terms of the acquisition but said in a statement that Tipp-Ex sales were 180 million francs in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;With our Wite-out brand in North America and Tipp-Ex, we'll own the world's best known brands in correcting fluid,&quot; chairman Bruno Bich said in the statement.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
